data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI'm currently focused on defining the scope by understanding the research questions. I've begun reviewing the six \"Pièce\" questions to grasp the overall goals. I am now working on ensuring I'm clear on each individual question.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 1841,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 127,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "j-gCa8GmNMCrxdIPi_XBuQc"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Structuring the Replies**\n\nI'm now methodically structuring the replies. I'm building out the framework to address each question precisely, using the specified headers (`Réponse 1`, `Réponse 2`, etc.). I have to ensure that I stay within the word limits for each one while making sure I address all the required aspects of the questions, like epistemic statuses and falsifiable statements.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 2128,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 414,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "j-gCa8GmNMCrxdIPi_XBuQc"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Analyzing the Examples**\n\nI'm now carefully analyzing historical examples to differentiate between attacks that are \"founded\" and those that are mere variants or assemblages. I am now trying to identify the critical criteria. For example, the difference between side-channel attacks and cryptanalytic variants, and the differences in Spectre/Meltdown compared to classical buffer overflows, is the key focus.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 2385,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 671,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "j-gCa8GmNMCrxdIPi_XBuQc"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Examining the ML Evidence**\n\nI'm now diving into the ML examples, specifically contrasting adversarial examples (like Szegedy et al., 2013) with mere noise or corruptions. I've compiled a quick list of key references from memory, starting with Kocher's seminal timing attacks paper. Next, I am thinking through the questions about LLMs and novel attack categories. I am hypothesizing that these might be mostly variants, but I'll need to test multi-LLM outputs against alternative methods to be sure.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 2682,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 968,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "j-gCa8GmNMCrxdIPi_XBuQc"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Testing New Attack Vectors**\n\nI'm now investigating a novel attack strategy. I'm focusing on whether a new strategy, S_new, induces an attack vector orthogonal to known attack representations. I plan to train linear probes and a text monitor on known strategies. I'll then measure the transfer loss of the new strategy, and assess whether fine-tuning recovers detection in the existing subspace. This will help determine if the new attack is a variant or represents a new category. I'm also considering the epistemic implications of these findings.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 2922,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 1208,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "j-gCa8GmNMCrxdIPi_XBuQc"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Proposing Distinct Candidates**\n\nI'm now proposing three distinct candidate attack categories, including scenarios where \"Aucune\" applies. The first, *Sabotage épistémique par sélection de cadre valide*, examines situations where every step is locally true and honest, but the methodology itself is suboptimal, akin to data poisoning or reward hacking. I'm focusing on key measures like KL-divergence and cosine similarity to validate this. I'll need to define control conditions to distinguish each.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 3128,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 1414,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "j-gCa8GmNMCrxdIPi_XBuQc"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Evaluating Error Rates**\n\nI'm now assessing the error rates in the attack categories. Specifically, the control for the sabotage candidate, a prompt injection variant, is failing to transfer. I am thinking of the tail-risk candidate and the functional steganography candidate, measuring the ratio of the audit statistical power to damage. I am also working on the control with uniform low-amplitude degradation.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 3303,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 1589,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "j-gCa8GmNMCrxdIPi_XBuQc"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Evaluating the Emergence**\n\nI'm now focusing on evaluating the emergence of the flaw. I'm measuring the Shapley value interaction index for higher-order interactions across steps. I am also testing the control, by shuffling or regenerating steps individually and checking for the collapse. The epistemic implications are a key aspect, since it would be possible to argue for \"Aucune\" depending on whether the category violates the underlying physical or computational model.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 3561,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 1847,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "j-gCa8GmNMCrxdIPi_XBuQc"}

data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Assessing Publication Timing**\n\nI'm now determining the optimal timing for publication, focusing on whether to release a short text before presenting results. I'm evaluating various content options, considering preregistration with cryptographic hashes, architectural overviews without specific implementations, and full disclosure of methods and benchmarks. I'm weighing the effects on recognition, scooping risk, measurement validity, adversary learning, and study quality, considering the implications for LLM training data and human red-teamers. I'm exploring the conditions under which early, delayed, or no publication would be most beneficial.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1714,"totalTokenCount": 3792,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 1714}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 2078,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-argon","responseId": "j-gCa8GmNMCrxdIPi_XBuQc"}

